  "goodToKnow": "Die Hymne is an anthem or hymn: die Nationalhymne, die Champions-League-Hymne. Since 1991, Germany's anthem has been only the third verse of the Deutschlandlied, which begins Einigkeit und Recht und Freiheit; the first verse is not sung because of its nationalist misuse. The melody is Joseph Haydn's (1797). The EU's anthem uses Beethoven's Ode an die Freude. The y sounds like ü: HÜM-ne. Plural: die Hymnen."
